icant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOUROGI MITSUHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NOMA TOMOYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI NORIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANEKA CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOUROGI, MITSUHARU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOMA, TOMOYA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, NORIYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOUROGI MITSUHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NOMA TOMOYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI NORIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOUROGI, MITSUHARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOMA, TOMOYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, NORIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A polyester resin composition which is excellent in mechanical properties, deflection temperature under load, surface appearance, dimensional stability, and releasability. The composition comprises a thermoplastic polyester resin and a phyllosilicate, wherein the phyllosilicate contained in the resin composition satisfies at least one of the following requirements (a) to (c): (a) the proportion of phyllosilicate particles having an equi-areal circle diameter, [D], of 3,000  ANGSTROM  or smaller is 20 % or higher, (b) the average of the equi-areal circle diameters [D] is 5,000  ANGSTROM  or smaller, and (c) the number of phyllosilicate particles, [N], present per 100  mu m&lt;2&gt; of the resin composition is 30 or larger.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition de résine polyester dotée de propriétés mécaniques efficaces et faisant preuve d'une température de déformation sous charge, d'un aspect de surface, d'une stabilité dimensionnelle et d'une capacité de détachement excellents. La composition renferme une résine polyester thermoplastique et un phyllosilicate remplissant au moins une des conditions requises suivantes: a) la proportion de particules de phyllosilicate ayant un diamètre de même aire (D) de 3000  ANGSTROM  au plus est de 20 % au moins, b) la moyenne des diamètres de même aire (D) est de 5000  ANGSTROM  au plus et c) le nombre de particules de phyllosilicate (N) par 100  mu m&lt;2&gt; de composition de résine est de 30 au moins.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>